plugin-qualify (0.5.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Version 0.5.1
  * native: install the interposer executable, so the RPM strips it and
    splits its debug info
  * DEB: recommend python3-lilv, which bookworm does not carry
  * Install check: run its steps in bash
  * Docs: the packages carry the CLAP prober, and where the command finds it
  * Packaging dry run: install the package and qualify the fixture plugins
    with nothing set
  * DEB: build the CLAP prober and its interposer into /usr/lib/plugin-qualify
  * RPM: build the CLAP prober and its interposer into
    %{_libexecdir}/plugin-qualify
  * Find the CLAP prober in the installed libexec directory before
    native/build
  * native: honour CPPFLAGS and LDFLAGS, add an install target

 -- Pau Aliagas <linuxnow@gmail.com>  Tue, 13 Oct 2026 01:38:19 +0000
